    :Namespace     ⍝ Anonymous
    ⍝ :Section Shortcut Definitions
    ⍝ Enter shortcut definitions
    ⍝ Here, for X, the letter (or letters) of the shortcut,
    ⍝ we store the function (in namespace ⎕SE.FString) as ⎕SE.FString.X.
    ⍝
    ⍝ If X_src does NOT exist, a code string is generated from the function
    ⍝   to be used when (inline: 1) is set or when a string is needed for internal functions.
    ⍝ If a variable X_src exists, it is expected to be a character vector
    ⍝   with the desired code, it will ber used in place of the string form of the function.
    ⍝ This X_src should be identical in operation to the function X, but may be far more
    ⍝ concise than a naive rendering.
    ⍝ See internal function Ð/Ð_src below for an example.
        
    ⍝ A: Above
    ⍝        a ∇ b: "obj a above obj b"
    ⍝          ∇ b: "blank line above obj b"
        A← {
            ⎕ML← 1 ⋄ ⍺← ⍬
            ⊃⍪/(⌈2÷⍨w-m)⌽¨f↑⍤1⍨¨m← ⌈/w← ⊃∘⌽⍤⍴¨f← ⎕FMT¨⍺⍵
        } 
    ⍝ B: Box
    ⍝     ∇ b: "box obj b"
    ⍝   a ∇ b: "a box b, where a are the options to APL ¨disp¨."
        B← {
            ⎕ML← 1 ⋄ d← |≡⍵ ⋄ ⍺← 0
            ⍺ ⎕SE.Dyalog.Utils.disp⊂⍣(1≥d),⍣(0=d)⊢⍵
        }  
        
    ⍝ C: Commas
    ⍝ Commas - Inserts a separator s (default ",") every n (default 5) digits in
    ⍝          the integer part of each right argument string.
    ⍝          You may enter no left arg or a left arg of: n, s, n s, or s n, with
    ⍝          omitted elements (n or s) replaced by the defaults.
    ⍝          Note: n is either an integer or a (character) digit.
    ⍝          These are the same:  "5_" and (5 "_").
    ⍝      Examples:
    ⍝          E.g.  { `C "123324"}     { 4 `C "123324"}     { 4 "_" `C "123324"}
    ⍝                { "_" `C "123324"} { "_" 4 `C "123324"}
    ⍝          Items omitted in the left arg will have their defaults: 3 ","
        C← { 
            ⎕IO ⎕ML← 0 1 ⋄ nd← ≢def← 3 ',' ⋄ ⍺← def 
            Opt← ⍕¨{                                 ⍝ Get options; def=defaults, o=options (⍺) 
                o← ⍵ ⋄ isN← (⎕D∊⍨ ⊃o)∨ 0=⊃0⍴o        ⍝ isN=1 if first option is <a number or digit>
              isN: o,(def↑⍨-0⌈nd-≢o) ⋄ (def↑⍨0⌈nd-≢o),⌽o    
            }  
            Esc← { ⍵≡⍥, '&': '\&' ⋄ ⍵/⍨1+ '\'= ⍵}    ⍝ Escapes. In case & or \ is the char separator
            n s← Opt ⍺
            src← '[.Ee]\d+',⍥⊂ '(?<=\d)(?=(\d{', n, '})+([-¯.Ee]|(?=\s|$)))'
            snk← '&',⍥⊂ '&',⍨ Esc s 
            w← src ⎕R snk⍤1 ⍕⍵
            ⊃⍣(1=≢⍵)⊢ w  
        } 
        
    ⍝ Ð: Internal box display (internal only)
        Ð← ⍎Ð_src← '0∘⎕SE.Dyalog.Utils.disp¯1∘↓' 
        
    ⍝ D: Date (or Time).
        D← {
            ⎕ML← 1 ⋄  ⍺← '%ISO%'
            ∊⍣(1=≡⍵)⊢⍺(1200⌶)⊢1⎕DT⊆⍵
        }
        
    ⍝ F: Format
        F← ⍎F_src← '⎕FMT' 
        
    ⍝ G: GetUrlText
    ⍝   lines@CVV ← [⍺←1] ∇ url
    ⍝   Retrieve URL ⍵ (assumes default 'https://' prefix, if prefix is omitted)
    ⍝   If ⍺=1, remove all html and scripts and return lines as a vector of CVs.
    ⍝   Otherwise return lines raw.
        G← {  
            ⍺← 1 
        ⍝  Loads HttpCommand (creates namespace) when first used...
            LoadHttp← { 
              0:: ⎕SIGNAL noCÊ   
                HttpCommand⊢← ()                     ⍝ Make empty ns in case Load fails.
                ⎕SE.SALT.Load 'HttpCommand'          ⍝ Try load.
            } 
            GetRaw← { ⍺← 1 
              0≥ ⍺: ⎕SIGNAL noCÊ                     ⍝ Only one try to load HttpCommand
                FullUrl← { ⍵,⍨ 'https://'/⍨~1∊'://'⍷⍵ } 
              9≠ ⎕NC 'HttpCommand':  0 ∇ ⍵ ⊣ LoadHttp⍬
                rec← HttpCommand.Get FullUrl ⍵
              rec.rc=  0: rec.Data 
              rec.rc= ¯1: ⎕SIGNAL badÊ
                ⎕SIGNAL nFÊ
            }
            noCÊ← ⊂('EN' 11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Http Commands are unavailable')   
            badÊ← ⊂('EN' 11)('Message' 'Invalid URL')
            nFÊ← ⊂('EN' 11)('Message' 'Unable to find URL') 
            pats repl← ↓⍉↑(
                '<script[^>]*>.*?</script[^>]*>' ''
                '<style[^>]*>.*?</style[^>]*>'   ''
                '<!-{0,2}.*?-->'                 ''
                '<[^>]+>'   ''
                '&amp;'     '&'
                '&lt;'      '<'
                '&gt;'      '>'
                '&quot;'    '"'
                '&nbsp;'    ' '
            )
            _Opts← ⍠('Mode' 'M')('DotAll' 1)
            Repl← pats ⎕R repl _Opts
            Split← (⎕UCS 10 13)∘((~∊⍨)⊆⊢)
            NoDup← '(\R\h*$)+'⎕R'\n'_Opts
            raw← GetRaw ⍵ 
          ⍺=0: raw ⋄ NoDup Split Repl raw 
        }           
        
    ⍝ J: Justify
        J← {
            ⎕PP← 34 
            ⍺← 'L' ⋄ B← {+/∧\' '=⍵}
            w⌽⍨(1⎕C⍺) { o← ⊂⍺                        ⍝ Treat ⍺ as a scalar.
              o∊'L'¯1: B ⍵
              o∊'R' 1: -B⌽⍵ 
              o∊'C' 0: ⌈0.5×⍵-⍥B⌽⍵                   ⍝ If o is invalid, drop off ends of earth.
                ⎕SIGNAL ⊂ ('EN' 11) ('Message' 'Shortcut option (⍺) was invalid')
            } w← ⎕FMT⍵
        }
        
    ⍝ £, `L: Library
    ⍝ Handled ad hoc as a niladic function
        
    ⍝ M: Merge
        M← {
            ⎕ML← 1
            ⍺← ⊢ ⋄ ⊃,/((⌈/≢¨)↑¨⊢)⎕FMT¨⍺⍵
        } 
        
    ⍝ Q: Quote
    ⍝      ∇ b: "Put single quotes around char. vectors/scalars in b"
    ⍝    a ∇ b: "Put our quotes around b as above,
    ⍝            with (⊃a) as the left quote char and (⊃⌽a) as the right."
        Q←  {
            ⍺← ''''               
          1<|≡⍵: ⍺∘∇¨⍵                              
          (0=⍴⍴⍵)∧1=≡⍵: ⍵                           
          (0≠≡⍵)∧326=⎕DR⍵: ⍺∘∇¨⍵                 
            ⎕ML← 1                                                                   
            ⍺{l r← ⍺ ⋄ 0=80|⎕DR⍵: l, r,⍨ ⍵/⍨ 1+r= ⍵ ⋄ ⍵}⍤1⊢⍵        
        }
        
    ⍝ S: Serialise (display in APLAN)
        S← { 
            ⎕ML← 1 ⋄ 11 16 6:: ⍵ ⋄ ⍺← 0     
          1=≢s← ⍺⎕SE.Dyalog.Array.Serialise⍵: ⊃s
            ⍪s
        }
    ⍝ T: Time or Date (aliases)
        T← D 
        
    ⍝ W: Wrap
        W← {
            ⎕ML← 1 ⋄ ⍺← ⎕UCS 39
          1<|≡⍵: ⍺∘∇¨⍵
            L R← 2⍴⍺ ⋄ {L,R,⍨⍕⍵}⍤1⊢⍵
        }
        
    ⍝ :EndSection Shortcut Definitions
    
    ⍝ :Section Futures Definitions
    ⍝ The required functions are shown below.
    ⍝ If not used, you must have at least a dummy function
    ⍝ e.g.     Ö← { 'Function not defined' ⎕SIGNAL 11 }
    ⍝   or     Ö← ⍎ Ö_src← '⊢'                       ⍝ A nop
    ⍝ Is the function is NOT in FUTURES, it won't be called no matter what the value.
        
    ⍝ Ö: Depth from Dyalog's dfns workspace
    ⍝ Recast as Ö.
    ⍝ Faster AFAIK than CircleDiaeresis below and not quite compatible.
    ⍝ See Also
    ⍝    CircleDiaeresis from Adam B's https://github.com/abrudz/dyalog_vision github.
    ⍝       MIT License
    ⍝    Copyright (c) 2018 Adám Brudzewsky
        Ö← {                                         ⍝ Apply fn ⍺⍺ at depths ⍵⍵.
            ⍺← ⊣
            depths← ⌽3⍴⌽⍵⍵                           ⍝ expand right operand
            m l r← depths-⍨(|≡¨⍵ ⍺ ⍵)×depths≥0       ⍝ ¨ digs top-down
            max encl← '¨⊂'⍴¨⍨l(⌈,∘|-)r               ⍝ find number of ¨s and ⊂s
            el er← (1 0=l≤r)/¨⊂encl                  ⍝ where do the ⊂s go?
          0:: ⎕SIGNAL ⎕EN                            ⍝ bubble errors up
            ⍎'(',el,'⍺)⍺⍺',max,er,'⍵'                ⍝ do it!
        }
        
    ⍝ ==================================================================================
        
    ⍝ Ë: By Adam B. under name Ellipsis.
    ⍝ See: https://github.com/abrudz/dyalog-apl-extended/blob/master/Ellipsis.dyalog
    ⍝ …  (⎕UCS 8230) Fill sequence gap (http://dfns.dyalog.com/n_to.htm)
        Ë← { 
            ⍺← ⊢
            ⍺{⎕IO← 0
                Char← 0 2∊⍨10|⎕DR                    ⍝ character?
                end← ⊃⍵                              ⍝ of sub-sequence
                tl← 1↓⍵                              ⍝ to be appended
                ce← Char end                         ⍝ character ⍵?
                deflt← ⎕UCS⍣ce⊢0                     ⍝ default beg from 0
                ⍺← deflt                             ⍝ deflt if monadic
                cb← Char¨¯2↑⍺                        ⍝ character ⍺?
                ld← -(2-ce)⌊(≢⍺)⌊+/ce=cb             ⍝ to be considered
                hd← ld↓⍺                             ⍝ to be prepended
                beg← (¯1⌊ld)↑¯2↑deflt,ld↑⍺           ⍝ first one/two items
              ce: hd,tl,⍨⎕UCS(⎕UCS beg)∇ ⎕UCS end    ⍝ char sequences
                from step← -⍨\2↑beg,beg+×end-beg     ⍝ step deflt is +/- 1
                hd,tl,⍨from+step×⍳0⌈1+⌊(end-from)÷step+step=0 ⍝ ⍺ thru ⍵ inclusive
            }⍤1⊢⍵ 
        }                                   
        
        
    ⍝ ==================================================================================
        
        
    ⍝ Î:  RtShoeUnder   (Indexing and Last)  (Def. by PMS)
    ⍝     [⍺] ⊇ ⍵
        Î← { 
            ⍺← ⊢ 
          0≢ ⍺ 0: ⍺⊂⍛⌷⍤0 99⊢ ⍵                       ⍝ Sane Indexing  ⌷⍨∘⊃⍨⍤0 99
            ⎕IO← 1                                   ⍝ Last...
          0= ≢⍴⍵: ⍵                                  ⍝ If scalar, return itself
          0= ≢⍵:  ⍵                                  ⍝ If empty array, return itself (or an empty prototype)
            ≢⍛⌷⍨ ⍵                                   ⍝ Otherwise, safely grab the last cell  
        }   
    ⍝ :EndSection Futures Definitions
 :EndNamespace 
